# Universe content · the grand tour: one flight from the whole visible universe down to the quarks, for watching
# Run it: Universe.exe --tour grand-tour (or Universe.exe --tour grand-tour). A click, the wheel or a key pauses it; T carries on, R starts again.
# Edit the stops to make your own. Each stop: do (shot, zoom, orbit, look, arc, fly, glide, pick) and its numbers. A shot
# frames what is picked by its own size: to-radii (how many of its sizes away) or to-km, sweep (degrees round it), rise
# (degrees up or down), seconds, max-rate (tenfolds of scale a second at most: never streaming past);
# through: yes flies on into the next stop without slowing or pausing; pan: degrees a second a zoom circles what it flies to
# (turn: degrees a second for the circling stops). There are no pauses: each caption stays on while the flight goes on.
# A caption of {sky} is written from what is really up from where you stand (its star only if it is in view, its moons, the
# other worlds, the galaxy's stars by night or the day sky by day).
# The film's grammar: an establishing shot; a straight push in or pull back to change scale; a calm circle only round what
# fills the view; looking round the sky from the ground slow (a few degrees a second at most, the sky turning too); a pan where it stands across what is vast; every move eased; circling 6 to 12 degrees a second; scale changing
# a third to a half of a tenfold a second; each shot 6 to 10 seconds. The director varies each shot every viewing.

@stop start
do: pick
target: start-galaxy
caption: Where we begin

@stop open
do: shot
to-radii: 6
sweep: 70
rise: 15
seconds: 9
caption: We begin beside a galaxy, a hundred billion stars turning in the dark

@stop leave
do: shot
to-km: 5e21
rise: 20
max-rate: 0.35
seconds: 8
caption: Pulling back: every point of light out here is a whole galaxy

@stop web
do: orbit
turn: 4
seconds: 10
caption: The cosmic web: galaxies along filaments and walls, round vast thin voids

@stop choose-galaxy
do: pick
target: far-galaxy
caption: A far galaxy

@stop cross
do: shot
to-radii: 8
sweep: 20
rise: 10
max-rate: 0.45
seconds: 8
caption: Across the universe, straight to one far away among a hundred billion

@stop round-galaxy
do: shot
to-radii: 3
sweep: 100
rise: -20
seconds: 10
caption: A hundred billion stars round a giant black hole

@stop bh
do: pick
target: black-hole
caption: A black hole

@stop to-bh
do: shot
to-radii: 60
sweep: 30
rise: 10
max-rate: 0.5
seconds: 8
caption: Down to the black hole at its heart

@stop round-bh
do: shot
to-radii: 25
sweep: 120
rise: 25
seconds: 10
caption: Its pull bends the light of the stars behind it; from inside its horizon nothing escapes

@stop choose-star
do: pick
target: star
caption: A star

@stop to-star
do: shot
to-km: 2e9
sweep: 20
max-rate: 0.5
seconds: 8
caption: Out to one star among them

@stop round-system
do: shot
to-km: 8e8
sweep: 100
rise: 30
seconds: 10
caption: The star, and the worlds born round it, each on its own tilted orbit

@stop asteroid
do: pick
target: asteroid
caption: An asteroid

@stop to-asteroid
do: shot
to-radii: 6
sweep: 20
max-rate: 0.5
seconds: 7
caption: Out to its belt of rubble

@stop round-asteroid
do: shot
to-radii: 3
sweep: 120
rise: 15
seconds: 8
caption: An asteroid: rock left over from when the worlds were made

@stop comet
do: pick
target: comet
caption: A comet

@stop to-comet
do: shot
to-km: 4e5
sweep: 30
rise: 10
max-rate: 0.5
seconds: 8
caption: A comet falling past its star, its tails streaming away from it

@stop near-comet
do: shot
to-radii: 15
sweep: 90
rise: -10
seconds: 9
caption: Into its coma: gas and dust boiling off a dark nucleus of ice

@stop star-2
do: pick
target: star
caption: Another star

@stop to-star-2
do: shot
to-km: 2e9
sweep: 20
max-rate: 0.5
seconds: 8
caption: Across light-years to another star

@stop round-star-2
do: shot
to-km: 8e8
sweep: 100
rise: 25
seconds: 9
caption: Another system, its worlds on their own orbits

@stop choose-planet
do: pick
target: planet
caption: A world

@stop to-planet
do: shot
to-radii: 5
sweep: 30
rise: 5
max-rate: 0.5
seconds: 8
caption: Down to one of its worlds

@stop round-planet
do: shot
to-radii: 2.5
sweep: 120
rise: 10
seconds: 10
caption: Seas, land, clouds and a thin shell of air

@stop to-land
do: zoom
rate: 0.5
until-km: 1.5
caption: Down through the air to the land

@stop over-hills
do: glide
rate: 0.5
turn: 3
seconds: 8
caption: Hills raised by moving plates, valleys worn by water

@stop to-head-height
do: zoom
rate: 0.35
until-km: 0.002
caption: Down to where a person stands

@stop stand
do: pick
target: none
caption: Standing

@stop look-up
do: look
tilt: 55
turn: 1.5
seconds: 10
caption: Look up

@stop sky
do: orbit
turn: 3
seconds: 12
caption: {sky}

@stop look-down
do: look
tilt: -85
turn: 1.5
seconds: 9
caption: And down: there is as much below us as above

@stop to-grains
do: zoom
rate: 0.4
until-km: 2e-6
through: yes
caption: The ground breaks into stones, then grains of sand

@stop choose-grain
do: pick
target: grain
caption: One grain of sand

@stop to-face
do: zoom
rate: 0.45
until-km: 2e-9
through: yes
caption: Onto one grain, a crystal of one mineral

@stop choose-spot
do: pick
target: spot
caption: A spot on its face

@stop to-crystal
do: zoom
rate: 0.5
until-km: 6e-12
caption: Down to its atoms, in a pattern repeated billions of times

@stop round-crystal
do: arc
rate: 0
until-km: 0
turn: 10
seconds: 8
caption: Round the atoms of the crystal, its lattice repeated billions of times

@stop into-lattice
do: arc
rate: 0.25
until-km: 1.5e-12
turn: 6
seconds: 5
caption: Down among them

@stop through-lattice
do: fly
rate: 0.6
turn: 3
seconds: 10
caption: Through the lattice: row on row of atoms, each bonded to its neighbours

@stop choose-atom
do: pick
target: atom
caption: One atom

@stop to-atom
do: zoom
rate: 0.4
until-km: 6e-13
caption: An atom is not a ball

@stop round-atom
do: arc
rate: 0.05
until-km: 2.5e-13
turn: 10
seconds: 8
caption: A tiny nucleus, its electrons round it, each in its own orbital's shape

@stop to-neighbour
do: pick
target: bonded-atom
caption: Its neighbour

@stop across-bond
do: arc
rate: 0
until-km: 0
turn: 8
seconds: 6
caption: Across the bond to its neighbour: atoms share their outer electrons

@stop choose-electron
do: pick
target: electron
caption: One electron

@stop follow-electron
do: arc
rate: 0
until-km: 0
turn: 10
seconds: 6
caption: An electron: a point, and a wave spread through its cloud

@stop choose-nucleus
do: pick
target: nucleus
caption: The nucleus

@stop to-nucleus
do: zoom
rate: 0.45
until-km: 3e-17
caption: Inward: an atom is almost all empty space

@stop round-nucleus
do: arc
rate: 0
until-km: 0
turn: 10
seconds: 7
caption: Its nucleus: protons and neutrons bound by the strong force

@stop choose-proton
do: pick
target: proton
caption: A proton

@stop to-proton
do: zoom
rate: 0.35
until-km: 2.5e-18
caption: Into a single proton

@stop round-proton
do: arc
rate: 0
until-km: 0
turn: 10
seconds: 8
caption: Three quarks in a storm of gluons

@stop choose-quark
do: pick
target: quark
caption: A quark

@stop to-quark
do: zoom
rate: 0.35
until-km: 6e-19
caption: One quark

@stop at-quark
do: orbit
turn: 8
seconds: 6
caption: The smallest thing we know

@stop let-go
do: pick
target: none
caption: And back out

@stop out-of-atom
do: zoom
rate: -0.7
until-km: 1e-9
caption: Back out through the atom, the crystal, the grain

@stop out-of-ground
do: zoom
rate: -0.7
until-km: 3e4
caption: Up from the ground, out of the air, away from the world

@stop out-of-system
do: zoom
rate: -0.7
until-km: 1e14
caption: Out past its star's worlds, its star a point among the galaxy's stars

@stop out-of-galaxy
do: zoom
rate: -0.6
until-km: 3e18
caption: Out of the galaxy, its hundred billion stars one spiral of light

@stop to-web
do: zoom
rate: -0.45
until-km: 5e21
caption: Out to the cosmic web, galaxies by the million

@stop end
do: orbit
turn: 4
seconds: 12
caption: The same universe at every scale, from the cosmic web to a quark
